@Keyrxng I tested the search query you use, and I think it is not reliable except if I am doing something wrong.
Here is my test:
https://github.com/search?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+repo%3Aubiquity%2Fubiquibot+in%3Abody+%22resolves+%231%22&type=pullrequests
As you can see in the results, comments in the body also match, which is wrong, can you confirm the same results happen in the code?
I don't think Github search API supports complex regexes to exclude these. Only advanced tool I know of is https://sourcegraph.com/. 
---
Edit: this scenario seems to be properly handled when using GraphQl. Example query (you can run it in their playground)
```gql
query {
  repository(owner: "ubiquity", name: "ubiquibot") {
    issue(number: 888) {
      id
      closedByPullRequestsReferences(first: 100, includeClosedPrs: true) {
        edges {
          node {
            id
            title
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Which returns the linked pull requests properly. Maybe this is more reliable? I cannot find the corresponding call in Rest API.

